course: dictionary
lesson: 10497
title: Tutor: a helper who teaches
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tutor is a teacher who teaches one pupil or a small group, often at home or after school. «Using AI to understand an idea, then doing the work yourself, is like having a patient tutor.» A patient tutor is someone who explains again and again without getting cross.
explain: Context clues tell you what a tutor does. «Used well, AI can be a patient tutor: explaining fractions a new way, quizzing your 7 and 8 times tables, or showing which spellings you got wrong.» The words after the colon are the clues: explaining, quizzing and showing mistakes are all things a tutor does.
explain: Tutor can also be a verb, meaning to teach someone in this way. In UK schools, «tutor time» means the start-of-day class meeting, so the words around the word tell you which meaning is being used.
fact: A tutor is a teacher who teaches one pupil or a small group, often at home or after school.
fact: «Private tutor» and «maths tutor» are phrases you may hear.
fact: In UK secondary schools, a form tutor looks after a class and takes the register.
fact: «Tutor time» or «tutor group» is the start-of-day class meeting in UK schools.
fact: To tutor means to teach someone in this way.
exercise: «Used well, AI can be a patient tutor: explaining fractions a new way, quizzing your 7 and 8 times tables, or showing which spellings you got wrong.» What does a tutor do in this sentence? | Cleans the classroom windows | Sells food at the school gate | *Explains, quizzes and shows mistakes | Plays football at break
exercise: «Using AI to understand an idea, then doing the work yourself, is like having a patient tutor.» What does patient mean here? | Quick to finish a task | Very loud and excited | *Willing to explain again without getting cross | Lying down and resting
exercise: In UK schools, «tutor time» is... | A lunchtime football match | *The start-of-day class meeting | A trip to the museum | A test at the end of term
test: «Her dad will tutor her in maths on Tuesdays.» What does tutor mean here? | To write a long letter | *To teach someone in this way | To lose track of time | To wash and dry dishes
test: Which person is a tutor? | A driver who takes people to the airport | A nurse who gives medicine in hospital | A cook who makes lunch for a whole school | *A teacher who helps one pupil at home
exam: «Sam's tutor showed him which spellings he got wrong.» What did the tutor do for Sam? | Took him to the park | Made his lunch | *Showed him which spellings he got wrong | Gave him a new bicycle
